#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# anger_j

#% text
# `anger_j(nu, z)` gives the Anger function `J_nu(z)`, the integral of `cos(nu*t - z*sin(t))` for `t` from 0 to `pi`, divided by `pi`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The definition is DLMF 11.10.1. For integer `nu` the Anger function equals `bessel_j(nu, z)`.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
anger_j(0.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.8551653096792622

#% cell
anger_j(1.5, 2.0)
#% output
#= 0.4036548767715669

#% cell
anger_j(2, 3.0) - bessel_j(2, 3.0)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The integral definition:

#% cell
n_integrate(cos(0.5*t - 1.0*sin(t)), [t, 0, pi])/pi - anger_j(0.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 2.220446049250313e-16

